  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Vulnerable Migrants in Tunisia with Assistance and Voluntary Return and Reintegration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In February 2023, Tunisian authorities adopted a new approach to irregular migration, leading to an increased demand for protection and assistance for vulnerable migrants in Tunisia, particularly for Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration (AVRR) to their countries of origin. IOM has witnessed a significant rise in requests for assistance, and by October 23, 2023, 1,863 returns were facilitated, surpassing the entire year of 2022. Closely with relevant stakeholders, we aim to strengthen the safeguarding of migrants in vulnerable situations, offering protection and assistance, including information on their rights and available options, with a focus on case management services and empowerment for durable solutions. The project includes providing short-term emergency assistance, vulnerability assessments, counselling on return options, and reintegration assistance for migrants, especially those rescued at sea, referred from land borders, and those in immigration detention. This initiative prioritizes migrant rights and well-being, striving to bridge the gap between arrival and reintegration while addressing medical cases.</narrative>
  </description>
